<title>SWITZERLAND: Novartis reports 1996 sales rise. [CORRECTED 01:15 GMT 29/1]</title>
<headline>Novartis reports 1996 sales rise. [CORRECTED 01:15 GMT 29/1]</headline>
<dateline>BASLE, Switzerland 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects headline to delete reference to 8 percent sales rise, which refers only to sales developments in the group's Life Sciences business segment and excludes sales developments in the group's divested operations, due to be spun off this year.)</p>
<p>Year Ended December 31, 1996</p>
<p>				    (million Sfr unless stated)</p>
<p> Group sales		    36,233	    vs 35,942</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of pharmaceuticals and chemical group is Novartis AG  </p>
<p>Sales by Business segment</p>
<p>    HEALTHCARE:		 16,272	    vs 15,011</p>
<p> Pharmaceuticals		12,184	    vs 11,216</p>
<p> Consumer Health		1,651	     vs 1,568</p>
<p>Generics 1,231 vs 1,106</p>
<p> CIBA Vision		    1,206	     vs 1,121 --</p>
<p>    AGRIBUSINESS:	     7,624	     vs 7,047</p>
<p> Crop Protection		5,594	     vs 5,117</p>
<p> Seeds			    1,189	     vs 1,083</p>
<p> Animal Health		  841		 vs 847</p>
<p>    NUTRITION:		  3,703	     vs 3,438</p>
<p> LIFE SCIENCES TOTAL	  27,599	    vs 25,496 --</p>
<p>CIBA SPECIALTY CHEMICALS:</p>
<p>				    6,623	     vs 6,325</p>
<p> Textile dyes		   1,173	     vs 1,083</p>
<p> Chemicals			990		 vs 911</p>
<p> Additives			2,065	     vs 2,067</p>
<p> Pigments			 1,073	     vs 1,026</p>
<p> Polymers			 1,322	     vs 1,238 --</p>
<p>    DIVERSIFIED OPERATIONS  2,011	     vs 4,121</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
